2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Exploring 'Mottainai' Culture and Eco-Friendly Experiences

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:15,108
Did you catch the morning news?

4
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:18,164
No, I didn’t.

5
00:00:18,187 --> 00:00:23,272
It was about Japan’s 'mottainai' culture.

6
00:00:23,295 --> 00:00:25,514
'Mottainai'? What’s that?

7
00:00:25,537 --> 00:00:27,989
What was the news about?

8
00:00:28,012 --> 00:00:32,546
It was about how Japanese culture values treasuring things.

9
00:00:32,569 --> 00:00:37,102
Japanese people really do cherish their belongings, don’t they?

10
00:00:37,125 --> 00:00:41,963
Eco experiences are super popular with foreigners, too.

11
00:00:41,987 --> 00:00:44,920
What kind of experiences are there?

12
00:00:44,943 --> 00:00:49,577
There’s a café that helps reduce food waste.

13
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,440
That’s a fantastic idea!

14
00:00:52,463 --> 00:00:56,263
They sell snacks that are close to their expiration date.

15
00:00:56,286 --> 00:00:59,486
And you can buy them at a discount, right?

16
00:00:59,509 --> 00:01:02,797
They have delicious cakes and bread, too.

17
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:06,154
It’s great because it prevents food from being wasted.

18
00:01:06,177 --> 00:01:09,675
They also offer 'kintsugi' experiences.

19
00:01:09,698 --> 00:01:11,832
Kintsugi? What’s that?

20
00:01:11,855 --> 00:01:15,421
It’s the art of repairing broken dishes.

21
00:01:15,444 --> 00:01:19,135
They mend them beautifully with gold.

22
00:01:19,159 --> 00:01:23,642
It creates a stunning new design.

23
00:01:23,665 --> 00:01:26,998
Recycling shops are popular, too.

24
00:01:27,021 --> 00:01:29,355
You mean secondhand clothing stores?

25
00:01:29,378 --> 00:01:33,378
They have so many nice clothes and bags.

26
00:01:33,401 --> 00:01:37,497
You can find great clothes at affordable prices.

27
00:01:37,521 --> 00:01:40,656
A lot of people carry their own water bottles, too.

28
00:01:40,679 --> 00:01:45,246
You can refill them at stations around the city.

29
00:01:45,269 --> 00:01:48,669
It helps reduce plastic waste.

30
00:01:48,692 --> 00:01:52,025
These are such eco-friendly initiatives!

31
00:01:52,048 --> 00:01:55,648
I’d love to try some of these eco experiences myself.

32
00:01:55,671 --> 00:02:00,038
Should we visit the food waste reduction café today?

33
00:02:00,061 --> 00:02:04,145
Yes, I’d love to go to that café!

34
00:02:04,168 --> 00:02:06,338
It’s in Shibuya.

35
00:02:06,362 --> 00:02:09,895
I’ll book a kintsugi experience, too.

36
00:02:09,918 --> 00:02:13,451
You can reserve it online.

37
00:02:13,474 --> 00:02:16,474
I’ll book it right now online.

38
00:02:16,497 --> 00:02:19,746
It’s reassuring to have a reservation.

39
00:02:19,770 --> 00:02:23,440
I’m excited to learn about Japan’s eco culture.

40
00:02:23,463 --> 00:02:26,796
Thanks for sharing the news with me!

41
00:02:26,819 --> 00:02:30,986
I can’t wait to enjoy Japan’s eco culture!

42
00:02:31,009 --> 00:02:34,609
Have a wonderful day!

43
00:02:34,632 --> 00:02:36,682
Thanks, I’m off!

44
00:02:36,705 --> 00:02:39,040
Take care, and have a great time!

