00:05:34,714 --> 00:05:36,214
Scene 3: Kintsugi Experience / Repairing with Gold

92
00:05:36,214 --> 00:05:38,261
Excuse me.

93
00:05:38,285 --> 00:05:42,552
Welcome to the Kintsugi experience workshop!

94
00:05:42,575 --> 00:05:44,941
Welcome!

95
00:05:44,964 --> 00:05:48,631
Please take a seat here.

96
00:05:48,654 --> 00:05:53,502
I'd like to beautifully repair this broken teacup.

97
00:05:53,526 --> 00:05:59,059
Yes, we can restore it beautifully with Kintsugi!

98
00:05:59,082 --> 00:06:03,249
This is my first time, so I'm a little nervous.

99
00:06:03,272 --> 00:06:07,155
Our craftsman will guide you carefully.

100
00:06:07,178 --> 00:06:09,468
I'm in your hands!

101
00:06:09,492 --> 00:06:14,292
First, we'll align the broken pieces.

102
00:06:14,315 --> 00:06:19,082
Let's assemble the pieces on the worktable.

103
00:06:19,105 --> 00:06:22,945
We'll use a special natural lacquer.

104
00:06:22,969 --> 00:06:26,444
We'll glue the pieces together with the lacquer?

105
00:06:26,467 --> 00:06:30,234
Yes, we'll bond it with lacquer.

106
00:06:30,257 --> 00:06:32,926
I'll apply it with a brush.

107
00:06:32,949 --> 00:06:35,716
Please coat the gaps carefully.

108
00:06:35,739 --> 00:06:38,672
I'll neatly fill in the gaps.

109
00:06:38,695 --> 00:06:43,373
Next, we'll sand the surface smooth with sandpaper.

110
00:06:43,397 --> 00:06:47,531
I'll gently sand it down.

111
00:06:47,554 --> 00:06:50,687
The surface is now smooth.

112
00:06:50,710 --> 00:06:53,524
A seam line has formed.

113
00:06:53,548 --> 00:06:58,081
Finally, we'll sprinkle real gold powder.

114
00:06:58,104 --> 00:07:01,152
I'll sprinkle the gold powder now.

115
00:07:01,176 --> 00:07:04,509
Lightly brush the powder into place.

116
00:07:04,532 --> 00:07:08,899
Oh, look—a beautiful gold line appeared!

117
00:07:08,922 --> 00:07:12,990
This turned into a stunning *kintsugi* piece.

118
00:07:13,014 --> 00:07:16,820
The cracks have become art.

119
00:07:16,843 --> 00:07:20,135
This embodies Japan’s *mottainai* culture—waste nothing.

120
00:07:20,158 --> 00:07:26,358
It really shows the spirit of treasuring what we have.

121
00:07:26,381 --> 00:07:29,436
You can take the repaired teacup home with you.

122
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:32,793
Can I take it home today?

123
00:07:32,816 --> 00:07:37,749
Yes, I’ll place it in a special case for you.

124
00:07:37,772 --> 00:07:40,782
How many days will it take to dry?

125
00:07:40,805 --> 00:07:45,263
It’ll take a few days to fully dry.

126
00:07:45,287 --> 00:07:48,557
I’ll let it dry carefully at home.

127
00:07:48,581 --> 00:07:52,853
Please avoid microwaves or dishwashers.

128
00:07:52,877 --> 00:07:56,488
I’ll wash it gently by hand.

129
00:07:56,512 --> 00:08:01,761
Cherish the teacup you repaired with your own hands.

130
00:08:01,785 --> 00:08:05,757
This was such a moving experience—I’m truly impressed!

131
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:10,064
I’m so glad you enjoyed it!

132
00:08:10,088 --> 00:08:13,969
Thank you for teaching me so patiently.

133
00:08:13,993 --> 00:08:16,126
Thank you!

134
00:08:16,149 --> 00:08:17,649
