530
00:29:42,890 --> 00:29:47,129
I want a T-shirt and a scarf towel.

531
00:29:47,152 --> 00:29:50,756
Please fill out the order form.

532
00:29:50,779 --> 00:29:53,913
I’ll check the items on the form.

533
00:29:53,936 --> 00:29:56,336
Please use a pen to write.

534
00:29:56,359 --> 00:29:59,959
What sizes are available for the T-shirts?

535
00:29:59,982 --> 00:30:04,915
We have S, M, and L sizes.

536
00:30:04,938 --> 00:30:08,433
I’ll take one M-sized T-shirt, please.

537
00:30:08,457 --> 00:30:12,261
One M-sized black T-shirt, correct?

538
00:30:12,285 --> 00:30:15,165
I’ll also take one scarf towel.

539
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:18,637
The towel with the red logo, right?

540
00:30:18,661 --> 00:30:22,194
Yes, I’ll take the red-logo towel, please.

541
00:30:22,217 --> 00:30:26,357
Do you have any limited-edition acrylic keychains?

542
00:30:26,380 --> 00:30:30,447
Yes, we still have keychains available.

543
00:30:30,470 --> 00:30:34,036
I’ll add two keychains as well.

544
00:30:34,059 --> 00:30:36,672
Two keychains, correct?

545
00:30:36,696 --> 00:30:39,829
Could you tell me the total amount?

546
00:30:39,852 --> 00:30:43,285
The T-shirt is 3,500 yen.

547
00:30:43,308 --> 00:30:46,083
The towel is 2,000 yen.

548
00:30:46,106 --> 00:30:49,763
The two keychains come to 1,600 yen.

549
00:30:49,787 --> 00:30:53,599
The total is 7,100 yen.

550
00:30:53,623 --> 00:30:57,833
Yes, your total is 7,100 yen.

551
00:30:57,856 --> 00:31:01,423
Can I pay with a credit card?

552
00:31:01,446 --> 00:31:05,213
Yes, cards are accepted.

553
00:31:05,236 --> 00:31:08,502
I’ll tap my card on the terminal.

554
00:31:08,525 --> 00:31:11,528
Your contactless payment is complete.

555
00:31:11,552 --> 00:31:14,519
Here are your items.

556
00:31:14,542 --> 00:31:16,178
Thank you!

557
00:31:16,201 --> 00:31:19,500
Please confirm the quantities.

558
00:31:19,524 --> 00:31:22,212
I’ll put them in a bag for you.

559
00:31:22,236 --> 00:31:26,334
I’ll wear this T-shirt to watch the concert.

560
00:31:26,357 --> 00:31:29,455
Is there a place to change into the T-shirt?

561
00:31:29,479 --> 00:31:33,656
There’s a changing area on the right side of the lobby.

562
00:31:33,680 --> 00:31:36,846
I’ll change and then watch the concert.

563
00:31:36,869 --> 00:31:40,403
Thank you so much for your kind assistance!

564
00:31:40,426 --> 00:31:42,426
Thank you!

565
00:31:42,449 --> 00:31:43,949
Scene 14: How to Exchange Your Drink Ticket

566
00:31:43,949 --> 00:31:45,919
Excuse me.

567
00:31:45,943 --> 00:31:50,310
I'd like to exchange this drink ticket for a beverage.

568
00:31:50,333 --> 00:31:52,066
Welcome!

569
00:31:52,089 --> 00:31:55,359
I'll take your ticket.

570
00:31:55,382 --> 00:31:58,059
Here's my drink ticket.

571
00:31:58,083 --> 00:31:59,650
Thank you!

572
00:31:59,673 --> 00:32:02,326
Please choose from the menu.

573
00:32:02,350 --> 00:32:05,184
What drinks do you have?

574
00:32:05,206 --> 00:32:09,140
We have draft beer and soft drinks.

575
00:32:09,163 --> 00:32:12,253
Can I get oolong tea?

576
00:32:12,277 --> 00:32:13,496
Yes.

577
00:32:13,519 --> 00:32:17,362
I can give you iced oolong tea.

578
00:32:17,386 --> 00:32:19,962
Do you have orange juice?

579
00:32:19,986 --> 00:32:21,201
Yes.

580
00:32:21,225 --> 00:32:25,058
We have 100% pure orange juice.

581
00:32:25,081 --> 00:32:27,815
Orange juice, please.

582
00:32:27,838 --> 00:32:30,073
Orange juice, coming right up.

583
00:32:30,096 --> 00:32:33,430
Should I put ice in the cup?

584
00:32:33,453 --> 00:32:34,910
Yes.

585
00:32:34,933 --> 00:32:37,576
Yes, with plenty of ice.

586
00:32:37,600 --> 00:32:41,167
Could I have less ice, please?

587
00:32:41,190 --> 00:32:42,430
Yes.

588
00:32:42,453 --> 00:32:45,390
I'll prepare it with less ice.

589
00:32:45,414 --> 00:32:48,014
I'll pour it into a plastic cup.

590
00:32:48,037 --> 00:32:49,841
Thank you!

591
00:32:49,864 --> 00:32:53,113
Here's your orange juice.

592
00:32:53,137 --> 00:32:55,270
Got it, thanks!

593
00:32:55,293 --> 00:32:58,026
It's in a plastic cup.

594
00:32:58,049 --> 00:33:03,382
Please grab a straw from the stand beside you. Okay, will do!

595
00:33:03,405 --> 00:33:06,839
You can bring it into the hall.

596
00:33:06,862 --> 00:33:09,944
You can drink it during the live performance.

597
00:33:09,967 --> 00:33:12,967
Please be careful not to spill it.

598
00:33:12,990 --> 00:33:15,869
What should I do with the cup when I'm done?

599
00:33:15,892 --> 00:33:18,743
Please throw it in the trash bin at the exit.

600
00:33:18,767 --> 00:33:22,100
Can I order more alcohol?

601
00:33:22,123 --> 00:33:23,359
Yes.

602
00:33:23,383 --> 00:33:27,950
A second drink can be ordered for 600 yen in cash.

603
00:33:27,973 --> 00:33:30,906
That's convenient—paying in cash!

604
00:33:30,929 --> 00:33:34,497
If you get thirsty again, please come back!

605
00:33:34,520 --> 00:33:37,320
I'll toss it in the collection box at the exit.

606
00:33:37,343 --> 00:33:38,676
Yes.

607
00:33:38,700 --> 00:33:41,233
Thank you for your cooperation!

608
00:33:41,256 --> 00:33:44,456
It's so cold and delicious!

609
00:33:44,479 --> 00:33:47,522
Enjoy the live to the fullest!

610
00:33:47,545 --> 00:33:50,979
Thank you for teaching me so patiently.

611
00:33:51,002 --> 00:33:52,968
Thank you!

612
00:33:52,991 --> 00:33:54,491
Scene 15: How to Buy Cheki (Photo) Tickets

613
00:33:54,491 --> 00:33:56,458
Excuse me.

614
00:33:56,481 --> 00:33:59,417
I'd like to buy a cheki ticket.

615
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:02,259
Welcome!

616
00:34:02,283 --> 00:34:05,083
Which member's cheki ticket would you like?

617
00:34:05,106 --> 00:34:09,519
I'll take Taka's cheki ticket, the vocalist.

618
00:34:09,542 --> 00:34:12,476
You want Taka's photo ticket, right?

619
00:34:12,499 --> 00:34:15,770
How much is one?

620
00:34:15,793 --> 00:34:19,126
It's 2,000 yen each.

621
00:34:19,149 --> 00:34:22,397
Can I buy two?

622
00:34:22,421 --> 00:34:27,755
Yes, you can buy up to two per person.

623
00:34:27,778 --> 00:34:29,945
I'll take two.

624
00:34:29,968 --> 00:34:32,839
That'll be 4,000 yen.

625
00:34:32,862 --> 00:34:36,429
Here's 4,000 yen in cash.

626
00:34:36,452 --> 00:34:39,585
I'll take the 4,000 yen.

627
00:34:39,608 --> 00:34:43,815
Here are your two cheki tickets.

628
00:34:43,838 --> 00:34:45,677
Thank you!

629
00:34:45,701 --> 00:34:48,840
Please line up for the photo session.

630
00:34:48,864 --> 00:34:52,349
Please line up at the end of the queue.

631
00:34:52,372 --> 00:34:54,246
Your turn will come up soon.

632
00:34:54,270 --> 00:35:00,448
When it's your turn, please hand your ticket to the photographer. Got it?

633
00:35:00,471 --> 00:35:03,745
Think about your pose in advance!

634
00:35:03,768 --> 00:35:07,202
I'd like to take a photo with a heart-shaped pose.

635
00:35:07,225 --> 00:35:10,158
Yes, I’m really looking forward to it!

636
00:35:10,181 --> 00:35:14,234
Enjoy your photo session with a big smile!

637
00:35:14,257 --> 00:35:18,475
It takes a few seconds for the photo to develop.

638
00:35:18,498 --> 00:35:22,232
The photo will appear from the white screen.

639
00:35:22,255 --> 00:35:26,526
After the photo is taken, the member will sign it for you.

640
00:35:26,550 --> 00:35:30,233
They'll add a signature and the date for you.

641
00:35:30,256 --> 00:35:34,489
The photo—your instant print—has appeared from the white background!

642
00:35:34,512 --> 00:35:37,605
The member will sign it now.

643
00:35:37,629 --> 00:35:40,686
They’ve added a signature and the date.

644
00:35:40,709 --> 00:35:43,643
Please treasure this keepsake!

645
00:35:43,666 --> 00:35:47,432
Please note that retakes aren’t possible.

646
00:35:47,455 --> 00:35:50,789
I’ll make sure not to blink.

647
00:35:50,812 --> 00:35:55,461
Yes, keep your eyes wide open for the perfect shot!

648
00:35:55,484 --> 00:35:58,525
Where should I put my belongings?

649
00:35:58,549 --> 00:36:02,616
Please place your belongings in the basket.

650
00:36:02,639 --> 00:36:05,273
I’ll put my things in the basket.

651
00:36:05,296 --> 00:36:08,995
Please proceed to the photo area.

652
00:36:09,018 --> 00:36:12,028
Thank you so much for guiding us!

653
00:36:12,052 --> 00:36:14,688
This will be a wonderful memory!

654
00:36:14,712 --> 00:36:17,930
Thank you for joining us!

655
00:36:17,953 --> 00:36:19,453
Scene 16: The Appeal of Cycling Tourism

656
00:36:19,453 --> 00:36:22,987
Did you catch the morning news?

657
00:36:23,010 --> 00:36:26,776
No, I didn’t.

658
00:36:26,799 --> 00:36:30,866
Now for some news on cycling tourism in rural areas.

659
00:36:30,889 --> 00:36:33,764
Cycling tourism?

660
00:36:33,787 --> 00:36:36,246
What was the news about?

661
00:36:36,269 --> 00:36:41,110
Rental bicycles are incredibly popular with foreign visitors.

662
00:36:41,134 --> 00:36:45,628
You can ride through some of the most scenic spots.

663
00:36:45,652 --> 00:36:51,285
You can rent e-bikes with electric assistance.

664
00:36:51,308 --> 00:36:55,741
E-bikes make hills a breeze!

665
00:36:55,765 --> 00:37:00,773
Popular routes include the Shimanami Kaido and Kyoto.

666
00:37:00,796 --> 00:37:04,405
Feeling the wind is so refreshing!

667
00:37:04,429 --> 00:37:08,288
There are even dedicated cycling paths.

668
00:37:08,311 --> 00:37:12,045
You can ride safely on these routes.

669
00:37:12,068 --> 00:37:16,038
You can rent bikes at tourist information centers.

670
00:37:16,061 --> 00:37:21,040
Can I drop off the bike at a different location?

671
00:37:21,063 --> 00:37:24,939
You can return it at another station.

672
00:37:24,962 --> 00:37:28,096
That’s so convenient!

673
00:37:28,119 --> 00:37:32,685
You can also rent helmets for free.

674
00:37:32,708 --> 00:37:35,846
Safety measures are thorough!

675
00:37:35,869 --> 00:37:40,803
You can rent a bike for around 1,500 yen per day.

676
00:37:40,826 --> 00:37:45,099
It’s an affordable way to explore!

677
00:37:45,122 --> 00:37:47,997
I want to go cycling today!

678
00:37:48,020 --> 00:37:52,420
Let’s head to the information center to rent a bike.

679
00:37:52,443 --> 00:37:56,510
You can also book online in advance.

680
00:37:56,533 --> 00:38:00,111
It’s reassuring to have a reservation.

681
00:38:00,135 --> 00:38:03,501
I’ll sign up online right now!

682
00:38:03,524 --> 00:38:07,604
Let’s ride along a scenic route!

683
00:38:07,628 --> 00:38:10,994
I’d love to ride along the coastal path.

684
00:38:11,017 --> 00:38:15,695
Let’s stop at a roadside station for some delicious ice cream!

685
00:38:15,719 --> 00:38:19,285
This is going to be an amazing cycling trip!

686
00:38:19,308 --> 00:38:22,275
Let's pack our things in the backpack.

687
00:38:22,298 --> 00:38:25,531
We should wear clothes that are easy to move in.

688
00:38:25,554 --> 00:38:28,600
I'll wear my sneakers.

689
00:38:28,624 --> 00:38:32,661
Don't forget to bring water for hydration.

690
00:38:32,684 --> 00:38:35,654
We're all set and ready to go!

691
00:38:35,677 --> 00:38:39,880
Let's ride safely and have fun!

692
00:38:39,904 --> 00:38:43,998
Thanks for sharing the news with me!

693
00:38:44,021 --> 00:38:48,088
I'll get the bikes ready and we'll head out.

694
00:38:48,111 --> 00:38:50,724
Yes, I'm really looking forward to it!

695
00:38:50,747 --> 00:38:52,247
Scene 17: Renting a Bicycle / How to Rent a Bicycle

696
00:38:52,247 --> 00:38:54,665
Excuse me.

697
00:38:54,689 --> 00:38:58,689
I'd like to rent a bicycle.

698
00:38:58,711 --> 00:39:00,716
Welcome!

699
00:39:00,740 --> 00:39:05,986
We have electric-assist bicycles available.

700
00:39:06,009 --> 00:39:09,776
Can I rent an e-bike?

701
00:39:09,799 --> 00:39:13,844
Yes, you can rent one.

702
00:39:13,867 --> 00:39:17,434
How much is it for one day?

703
00:39:17,457 --> 00:39:21,635
It's 1,500 yen per day.

704
00:39:21,658 --> 00:39:24,425
1,500 yen, got it.

705
00:39:24,448 --> 00:39:29,615
Do I need to return it by 5 PM?

706
00:39:29,638 --> 00:39:33,708
Yes, please return it by 5 PM.

707
00:39:33,731 --> 00:39:37,464
I'll fill out the application form.

708
00:39:37,487 --> 00:39:42,054
Please write your name and phone number on the form.

709
00:39:42,077 --> 00:39:45,010
I've filled out the form.

710
00:39:45,033 --> 00:39:48,836
Could you show me your ID, please?

711
00:39:48,860 --> 00:39:51,515
Here's my passport.

712
00:39:51,538 --> 00:39:54,705
Your passport checks out.

713
00:39:54,728 --> 00:39:58,295
I'll pay in cash.

714
00:39:58,318 --> 00:40:02,087
I'll take the 1,500 yen.

715
00:40:02,110 --> 00:40:06,177
Here's the bike key and your receipt.

716
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:07,733
Thank you!

717
00:40:07,756 --> 00:40:11,090
Your bike is ready outside.

718
00:40:11,113 --> 00:40:14,601
Is the battery fully charged?

719
00:40:14,624 --> 00:40:19,101
Yes, it's 100% charged.

720
00:40:19,124 --> 00:40:22,924
Could you show me how to turn it on?

721
00:40:22,947 --> 00:40:26,681
Just press and hold the button on the handle.

722
00:40:26,704 --> 00:40:31,306
When I pressed the button, the light and meter turned on.

723
00:40:31,330 --> 00:40:36,163
Switch to strong mode when going uphill.

724
00:40:36,186 --> 00:40:39,923
This will make climbing hills so much easier!

725
00:40:39,947 --> 00:40:44,613
Safety first—please wear your helmet.

726
00:40:44,636 --> 00:40:47,270
Got it!

727
00:40:47,293 --> 00:40:51,628
I'll also give you a recommended cycling map.

728
00:40:51,651 --> 00:40:54,584
I received a sightseeing map.

729
00:40:54,607 --> 00:40:57,941
We'll ride along a scenic route.

730
00:40:57,964 --> 00:41:01,842
Please ride on the left side of the road.

731
00:41:01,866 --> 00:41:04,753
I'll be careful of cars while riding.

732
00:41:04,776 --> 00:41:09,417
The light turns on automatically when it gets dark.

733
00:41:09,441 --> 00:41:12,445
Automatic lights are so reassuring!

734
00:41:12,468 --> 00:41:15,638
Be careful and have a safe ride!

735
00:41:15,662 --> 00:41:19,329
Thank you for the detailed explanation.

736
00:41:19,352 --> 00:41:21,637
Thank you!

737
00:41:21,660 --> 00:41:23,160
Scene 18: Helmet Size Adjustment / Helmet Size Adjustment

738
00:41:23,160 --> 00:41:25,593
Excuse me.

739
00:41:25,616 --> 00:41:29,434
I'd like to adjust the helmet size.

740
00:41:29,457 --> 00:41:31,124
Welcome!

741
00:41:31,147 --> 00:41:35,033
Please try on this helmet.

742
00:41:35,056 --> 00:41:38,751
I'll try on the medium-sized helmet.

743
00:41:38,774 --> 00:41:42,041
Does it fit your head properly?

744
00:41:42,065 --> 00:41:45,721
It feels a bit tight width-wise.

745
00:41:45,745 --> 00:41:50,318
I'll bring you a size L helmet then.

746
00:41:50,341 --> 00:41:52,819
I'll try the L size.

747
00:41:52,843 --> 00:41:55,409
How does the L size feel?

748
00:41:55,432 --> 00:41:59,076
The L size fits perfectly and doesn't hurt.

749
00:41:59,100 --> 00:42:03,933
Please turn the adjuster at the back.

750
00:42:03,957 --> 00:42:07,199
I'll turn the dial to the right.

751
00:42:07,223 --> 00:42:10,256
It fits snugly on your head now.

752
00:42:10,279 --> 00:42:14,212
Would you like to adjust the chin strap length as well?

753
00:42:14,235 --> 00:42:15,604
Yes.

754
00:42:15,628 --> 00:42:20,324
Leave enough room to fit one finger under your chin.

755
00:42:20,347 --> 00:42:23,114
I'll fasten the buckle for you.

756
00:42:23,137 --> 00:42:25,419
Does it wobble at all?

757
00:42:25,443 --> 00:42:28,134
It doesn't shift even when I shake my head.

758
00:42:28,157 --> 00:42:31,563
The fit is just right now.

759
00:42:31,586 --> 00:42:36,801
Is wearing a helmet mandatory when cycling in Japan?

760
00:42:36,825 --> 00:42:38,158
Yes.

761
00:42:38,181 --> 00:42:42,648
Helmet use is strongly encouraged, but not mandatory.

762
00:42:42,672 --> 00:42:46,805
Safety first—I'll always wear one while riding.

763
00:42:46,828 --> 00:42:47,995
Yes.

764
00:42:48,018 --> 00:42:52,151
It protects your head in case of a fall.

765
00:42:52,174 --> 00:42:55,553
How much is the helmet rental?

766
00:42:55,576 --> 00:42:58,949
The helmet rental is free.

767
00:42:58,972 --> 00:43:02,806
It's great that I can borrow it for free!

768
00:43:02,829 --> 00:43:07,162
Don't worry—it's been sanitized for cleanliness.

769
00:43:07,185 --> 00:43:10,919
Do you have helmets in black and white?

770
00:43:10,942 --> 00:43:12,075
Yes.

771
00:43:12,098 --> 00:43:15,431
We have helmets in both black and white.

772
00:43:15,454 --> 00:43:18,687
I'll go with the white helmet.

773
00:43:18,710 --> 00:43:21,397
Here's your white helmet.

774
00:43:21,421 --> 00:43:25,271
I'll borrow the size L helmet.

775
00:43:25,294 --> 00:43:29,661
Please ride safely on the left side of the road.

776
00:43:29,684 --> 00:43:31,925
I'll ride on the left.

777
00:43:31,949 --> 00:43:34,786
Take care and have a safe ride!

778
00:43:34,809 --> 00:43:38,575
Thank you for adjusting it so carefully.

779
00:43:38,598 --> 00:43:40,732
Thank you!

780
00:43:40,755 --> 00:43:42,255
Scene 19: How to Find Cycling Routes

781
00:43:42,255 --> 00:43:44,111
Excuse me.

782
00:43:44,134 --> 00:43:48,822
I'd like to know about recommended cycling routes.

783
00:43:48,845 --> 00:43:50,578
Welcome!

784
00:43:50,601 --> 00:43:54,445
Please take a look at this dedicated map.

785
00:43:54,469 --> 00:43:59,715
Where is the bike-only road?

786
00:43:59,739 --> 00:44:05,672
The blue-lined path along the river is a bike-only road.

787
00:44:05,695 --> 00:44:10,662
It's safe since no cars come through.

788
00:44:10,685 --> 00:44:15,754
Yes, it's a car-free route, so you can ride with peace of mind.

789
00:44:15,778 --> 00:44:20,517
Can I go on a route with ocean views?

790
00:44:20,540 --> 00:44:25,425
Yes, the coastal route offers stunning views and comes highly recommended.

791
00:44:25,448 --> 00:44:28,782
How many kilometers is the round trip?

792
00:44:28,805 --> 00:44:33,879
The round trip is about 15 kilometers—great for beginners.

793
00:44:33,902 --> 00:44:39,435
I can ride 15 kilometers in about two hours.

794
00:44:39,458 --> 00:44:44,425
E-bikes make climbing hills a breeze.

795
00:44:44,448 --> 00:44:48,281
Are there rest stops along the way?

796
00:44:48,304 --> 00:44:53,114
There are roadside stations and cafés every 5 kilometers.

797
00:44:53,138 --> 00:44:56,671
I'd love to try soft-serve ice cream at a café.

798
00:44:56,694 --> 00:45:00,869
The local fresh milk ice cream is delicious!

799
00:45:00,892 --> 00:45:05,092
Are the road signs easy to understand?

800
00:45:05,115 --> 00:45:10,788
Yes, there are blue arrows on the road for guidance.

801
00:45:10,812 --> 00:45:14,587
Just follow the blue arrows—you won’t get lost!

802
00:45:14,611 --> 00:45:18,488
There’s even a smartphone holder on the bike.

803
00:45:18,511 --> 00:45:21,878
We’ll ride while checking the map on our phones.

804
00:45:21,901 --> 00:45:27,934
Please watch out for pedestrians too.

805
00:45:27,957 --> 00:45:30,560
Slow down in crowded areas.

806
00:45:30,584 --> 00:45:34,865
Ride slowly without ringing the bell, please.

807
00:45:34,888 --> 00:45:37,921
Safety first—let’s enjoy the ride!

808
00:45:37,944 --> 00:45:41,957
Hope you enjoy the breathtaking views!

809
00:45:41,981 --> 00:45:45,314
Are there restrooms along the route?

810
00:45:45,337 --> 00:45:50,737
Yes, there are clean restrooms at parks and roadside stations.

811
00:45:50,760 --> 00:45:54,294
Plenty of restrooms—so convenient!

812
00:45:54,317 --> 00:45:57,693
There are lots of vending machines too.

813
00:45:57,716 --> 00:46:02,590
You can grab water for hydration anytime.

814
00:46:02,614 --> 00:46:05,697
Remember to stay hydrated!

815
00:46:05,721 --> 00:46:08,287
Are there any photo spots?

816
00:46:08,310 --> 00:46:13,377
The ocean-view observation deck is a must-visit for photos!

817
00:46:13,400 --> 00:46:17,276
I’ll take some great shots at the observation deck.

818
00:46:17,299 --> 00:46:20,766
You’ll get amazing photos there!

819
00:46:20,789 --> 00:46:24,356
Thank you for teaching me so patiently.

820
00:46:24,379 --> 00:46:26,712
Take care, and have a great time!

821
00:46:26,735 --> 00:46:28,235
Scene 20: Bicycle Return Procedure

822
00:46:28,235 --> 00:46:30,205
Excuse me.

823
00:46:30,228 --> 00:46:33,362
I’d like to return the bicycle.

824
00:46:33,385 --> 00:46:35,518
Welcome back!

825
00:46:35,541 --> 00:46:40,008
We’ll process the return at this station.

826
00:46:40,031 --> 00:46:45,231
I rented it elsewhere—can I return it here?

827
00:46:45,254 --> 00:46:46,854
Yes.

828
00:46:46,876 --> 00:46:50,365
This is a one-way drop-off station.

829
00:46:50,388 --> 00:46:53,764
I’ll park the bike in the rack.

830
00:46:53,787 --> 00:46:57,457
Please align the wheels within the frame.

831
00:46:57,481 --> 00:47:00,314
Lock the bike with the key.

832
00:47:00,337 --> 00:47:01,613
Yes.

833
00:47:01,637 --> 00:47:04,707
The lock is confirmed secure.

834
00:47:04,730 --> 00:47:09,768
The battery is at 20% remaining.

835
00:47:09,792 --> 00:47:14,078
You had a full day of riding!

836
00:47:14,102 --> 00:47:17,269
Here’s your helmet and receipt back.

837
00:47:17,292 --> 00:47:20,625
We’ll take your helmet and receipt.

838
00:47:20,648 --> 00:47:23,521
Here’s the key as well.

839
00:47:23,544 --> 00:47:26,077
Key received.

840
00:47:26,100 --> 00:47:29,434
Is there an extra fee for one-way drop-off?

841
00:47:29,457 --> 00:47:33,533
You’ve already paid the one-way fee in advance.

842
00:47:33,556 --> 00:47:36,494
No additional charges, right?

843
00:47:36,518 --> 00:47:37,992
Yes.

844
00:47:38,015 --> 00:47:40,688
No extra payment is needed.

845
00:47:40,711 --> 00:47:44,982
Check for any forgotten items on the bike.

846
00:47:45,006 --> 00:47:49,372
Please check the front basket and under the saddle.

847
00:47:49,395 --> 00:47:52,595
Nothing left in the basket.

848
00:47:52,618 --> 00:47:55,952
Please check under the saddle too.

849
00:47:55,975 --> 00:47:58,741
Checked under the saddle—all clear.

850
00:47:58,764 --> 00:48:01,298
No forgotten items.

851
00:48:01,321 --> 00:48:04,364
Return procedure complete.

852
00:48:04,388 --> 00:48:08,721
We saw incredible scenery on this cycling trip!

853
00:48:08,744 --> 00:48:12,781
Perfect weather for an amazing ride!

854
00:48:12,805 --> 00:48:16,338
What are the local specialties at this roadside station?

855
00:48:16,361 --> 00:48:21,565
Fresh orange juice and soft-serve ice cream are famous here!

856
00:48:21,589 --> 00:48:24,923
I’ll grab some delicious orange juice to drink!

857
00:48:24,946 --> 00:48:27,550
You can find them at our souvenir corner!

858
00:48:27,574 --> 00:48:30,625
I'll definitely grab some local snacks to take home.

859
00:48:30,648 --> 00:48:34,381
Be sure to savor the authentic local flavors!

860
00:48:34,404 --> 00:48:38,538
Thanks to the rental bike, this turned out to be an amazing day!

861
00:48:38,561 --> 00:48:42,694
We sincerely look forward to welcoming you back again.

862
00:48:42,717 --> 00:48:45,152
Where can I find the bus stop?

863
00:48:45,176 --> 00:48:49,709
The bus stop is right in front of the main entrance of the roadside station.

864
00:48:49,732 --> 00:48:52,067
I'll take the bus back to the station.

865
00:48:52,090 --> 00:48:55,224
Please take care on your way home.

866
00:48:55,247 --> 00:48:58,425
Thank you so much for your thorough assistance with the process.

867
00:48:58,448 --> 00:49:00,848
Thank you!